# Trivy ignore list for the CI "Trivy scan" job (docker build -t scan-target
# headscale/ + trivy image scan, severity HIGH,CRITICAL, ignore-unfixed).
#
# Every entry below is a HIGH/CRITICAL CVE in the Go stdlib or a Go module
# baked into a THIRD-PARTY upstream binary this addon copies verbatim from
# its pinned base images (ghcr.io/hassio-addons/base, ghcr.io/juanfont/
# headscale, ghcr.io/tale/headplane, tailscale/tailscale) — none of it is
# our own source code, and each pinned image tag below was confirmed (at
# the time this file was written) to already be the latest release
# published upstream, so there is no newer tag in our tree to bump to.
# Dependabot's `docker` ecosystem watch on headscale/Dockerfile (plus the
# weekly `scheduled.yaml` rebuild-and-diff job) will pick up new upstream
# releases automatically; a maintainer should re-run `trivy image
# scan-target` after any such bump and prune entries that are now fixed.

